    "solution": "Jump and dash under the western partition onto the small pod island. Stop there and line up above the pod. Jump, then dash down into it: the pod reverses the dash into a stronger upward throw and returns the spent dash. Use that fresh dash upward while still rising; this removes the high phase ceiling so you can pass through it. Cut upward at the bell to restore the same surface beneath you. Land on the broad bridge and walk along the safe eastern gallery.",
    "nearestExisting": "F34 combines a wallbounce and an aerial phase bell. Here a down-dash first buys an upward pressure-pod return and a fresh dash; that returned resource must then open the ceiling during the rise. The original western-pillar route and the ordinary jump-dash from the pod island both bypassed this idea and are now saved as successful-before/failing-after regressions.",
    "novelty": "The direction reversal and returned dash solve different parts of the same crossing: the pod supplies height, the next dash removes the ceiling, and the blade restores the landing. The clear downward entry replaces the former hard-to-read diagonal approach.",
